  "chapter": {
    "number": 100,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(101) A Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will sing to you, O Lord, of mercy and judgment; I will sing a psalm,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and I will be wise in a blameless way. When will you come to me? I walked in the innocence of my heart, in the midst of my house.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have not set before my eyes any unlawful thing; I have hated transgressors.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "A perverse heart has not cleaved to me; I have not known an evil man, forasmuch as he turns away from me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Him that privily speaks against his neighbor, him have I driven from me: he that is proud in look and insatiable in heart, —with him I have not eaten.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "My eyes shall be upon the faithful of the land, that they may dwell with me: he that walked in a perfect way, the same ministered to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The proud doer lived not in the midst of my house; the unjust speaker prospered not in my sight.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Early did I kill all the sinners of the land, that I might destroy out of the city of the Lord all that work iniquity.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
